⨯ keywords: `uint32` is a keyword and may not be used as an identifier
  @ test.idl:2:14

 2 │ typedef long uint32;
   │              ˆˆˆˆˆˆ this is an IDL keyword
 3 │ typedef boolean octet;

  ? the keyword can be escaped by changing to `_uint32`
  * keywords are matched case-insensitively against identifiers

⨯ keywords: `octet` is a keyword and may not be used as an identifier
